Stack Solution
Approach:
Create an empty stack to store the values of the linked list.
Traverse the linked list and push every node's value onto the stack.
Reset the pointer to the head of the linked list.
Traverse the list again while popping elements from the stack.
Compare the current node's value with the top of the stack.
If any value does not match, return false.
If all values match, return true, indicating that the linked list is a palindrome.

Time Complexity: O(n)

One traversal to push all elements into the stack.
One traversal to compare elements.

Space Complexity: O(n)

The stack stores all n node values.
class Solution {
public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {

        // Stack to store node values
        stack<int> st;

        ListNode* temp = head;

        // Push all node values into the stack
        while(temp != NULL){
            st.push(temp->val);
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        // Compare stack values with linked list
        temp = head;

        while(temp != NULL){
            if(temp->val != st.top()){
                return false;
            }
            st.pop();
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        return true;
    }
};


Optimal Solution (Reverse Second Half)
Approach:
Handle the edge case where the linked list has 0 or 1 node, as it is always a palindrome.
Use slow and fast pointers to find the middle of the linked list.
Reverse the second half of the linked list.
Compare the nodes from the first half and the reversed second half.
If any pair of nodes has different values, restore the original linked list by reversing the second half again and return false.
After successful comparison, reverse the second half again to restore the original linked list.
Return true if all corresponding nodes match.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Finding the middle: O(n/2)
Reversing the second half: O(n/2)
Comparing both halves: O(n/2)
Restoring the list: O(n/2)

Overall: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(1)

The linked list is modified in-place without using any extra data structure.
class Solution {

private:
    ListNode* reverse(ListNode* head){
        ListNode* prev = nullptr;
        ListNode* curr = head;

        while(curr != nullptr){
            ListNode* nextNode = curr->next;
            curr->next = prev;
            prev = curr;
            curr = nextNode;
        }

        return prev;
    }

public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {

        if(head == nullptr || head->next == nullptr){
            return true;
        }

        // Find the middle of the linked list
        ListNode* slow = head;
        ListNode* fast = head;

        while(fast->next != nullptr && fast->next->next != nullptr){
            slow = slow->next;
            fast = fast->next->next;
        }

        // Reverse the second half
        ListNode* newHead = reverse(slow->next);

        // Compare both halves
        ListNode* first = head;
        ListNode* second = newHead;

        while(second != nullptr){
            if(first->val != second->val){
                reverse(newHead);   // Restore original list
                return false;
            }

            first = first->next;
            second = second->next;
        }

        // Restore original list
        reverse(newHead);

        return true;
    }
};

